            <ArticleTitle>Left ventricular free wall rupture after coronary artery surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>499-500</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient who had undergone urgent coronary artery bypass grafting for unstable angina developed a fatal left ventricular free wall rupture in the early postoperative period. Heart rupture following surgical revascularisation has not been reported before.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
